Aside: Standard SVGD
Let \pi be a target density on \mathbb{R}^d, Q a current particle law, and let \mathcal H_K be a vector-valued RKHS of vector fields \phi:\mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}^d with matrix kernel K:\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}. The Langevin Stein operator on vector fields is 
\big(\mathcal S^{\mathrm{Lan}}_\pi \phi\big)(x) = \nabla\cdot\phi(x) +\phi(x)^\top \nabla \log \pi(x)

First variation of KL (explicit form)
Consider the transport T_\varepsilon(x)=x+\varepsilon\,\phi(x) and the pushed law Q_\varepsilon=(T_\varepsilon)_\# Q. A calculation (change of variables + integration by parts) gives 
\left.\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\mathrm{KL}(Q_\varepsilon|\pi) \right|_{\varepsilon=0} \;=\; -\,\mathbb E_{x\sim Q}\Big[\,\nabla\cdot\phi(x) + \phi(x)^\top \nabla \log \pi(x)\,\Big]
= -\mathbb E_{Q}\big[\mathcal S^{\mathrm{Lan}}_\pi \phi\big].
\tag{1}

To work in \mathcal H_K, use the reproducing identities (for any z\in\mathbb{R}^d and v\in\mathbb{R}^d): 
\langle \phi,K(\cdot,z)\,v\rangle_{\mathcal H_K}= v^\top \phi(z),
\qquad
\langle \phi,\nabla_z K(\cdot,z)\rangle_{\mathcal H_K}= \nabla\cdot\phi(z),
\tag{2}
 where \nabla_z K(\cdot,z)\in \mathcal H_K is the \mathcal H_K member whose inner product with \phi equals \nabla \cdot \phi(z). Combining (1)–(2), 
\left.\frac{d}{d\varepsilon}\mathrm{KL}(Q_\varepsilon|\pi)\right|_{\varepsilon=0}
= -\,\Big\langle \phi,
\mathbb E_{x\sim Q}\big[\,K(\cdot,x)\nabla \log \pi(x) + \nabla_x K(\cdot,x)\,\big]\Big\rangle_{\mathcal H_K}.
\tag{3}

Thus the (unconstrained) steepest descent direction is the field \phi that appears inside the bracket on the right-hand side of (3): 
\boxed{\;
\phi_{\mathrm{SVGD}}(z) =
\mathbb E_{x\sim Q}\big[\,K(z,x)\,\nabla\log \pi + \nabla_x K(z,x)\,\big].
\;}
\tag{4}
 The practical particle update is x_i \leftarrow x_i + \varepsilon\,\phi_{\mathrm{SVGD}}(x_i).
Squared KSD
Define the (Langevin) kernel Stein discrepancy by the operator norm over the RKHS unit ball: 
D_{\mathcal S}(Q|\pi)
\;:=\;
\sup_{|\phi|_{\mathcal H_K}\le 1}\;
\mathbb E_{X\sim Q}\big[\mathcal S^{\mathrm{Lan}}_\pi \phi(X)\big].
\tag{5}

By Cauchy–Schwarz in \mathcal H_K, 
D_{\mathcal S}(Q|\pi)^2
\;=\;
\left\|\mathbb E_{x\sim Q}\big[\,K(\cdot,x)\,\nabla\log \pi(x) + \nabla_x K(\cdot,x)\big]\,\right\|_{\mathcal H_K}^2.
\tag{6}

Expanding the RKHS norm gives the familiar double-expectation closed form with the Stein kernel
\begin{align*}
k_0(x,x') & :=\; \nabla\log \pi(x)^\top K(x,x')\,\nabla\log \pi(x') + \nabla\log \pi(x)^\top \nabla_{x'} K(x,x') \\ & \qquad +  \big(\nabla_{x} K(x,x')\big)^\top \nabla\log \pi(x')  + \mathrm{tr}\big(\nabla_{x}\nabla_{x'}^\top K(x,x')\big),
\end{align*}
namely 
\boxed{
D_{\mathcal S}(Q|\pi)^2 =
\mathbb E_{x,x'\sim Q}\big[k_0(x,x')\big].
}
\tag{7}
